.TH HUSH 1 "" "hush" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hush \- a trinary notifications filter, placement, and tray icon for mako
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dnd-comms-toggle
.RB [ toggle | status | "set " STATE ]
.br
.B mako-placement
.br
.B comms-indicator
.RB [ render-test " " DIR ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
hush is a small notifications suite over
.BR mako (1).
There is no eponymous
.B hush
command; the three tools below are invoked by name (the tray icon runs as a
.B --user
service).
.PP
The FILTER is trinary and application-based, not identity-based: it cycles a
mako mode set so notifications flow, or only "work" flows (personal muted), or
all are muted. What counts as work vs personal is a mako rule (e.g. Slack vs
Signal), so hush carries no notion of a work account or boundary.
.SH TOOLS
.TP
.B dnd-comms-toggle
The filter state machine. `toggle` cycles all -> work -> none; `set <state>`
jumps to one; a bare call prints the state as waybar JSON. It drives mako via
.BR makoctl " mode."
State lives in
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/dnd-comms-state .
.TP
.B mako-placement
Writes the notification placement/sizing to mako's
.I placement.active
include for the current display. It reads the per-shape
.I ~/.config/shapes/<shape>/mako.conf
and the display density when a shape resolver (kanshi-autoscale) is present, and
falls back to a shipped single-output default otherwise. Both are OPTIONAL soft
dependencies; hush degrades cleanly without them.
.TP
.B comms-indicator
An SNI tray icon drawn as an owned glyph (a rounded tile, frame colour = state).
It reads the filter state to draw and left-click cycles it via
.BR dnd-comms-toggle .
Runs as the
.I comms-indicator.service
.B --user
unit (a venv-backed Python daemon; needs a tray host).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mako/config
hush's mako config (appearance + the dnd modes); include's placement.active.
.TP
.I ~/.config/shapes/<shape>/mako.conf
Optional per-shape placement/sizing (a shared, integrator-owned tree); read when
present.
.SH RUNTIME DEPENDENCIES
.BR mako "(1), " makoctl "(1); a StatusNotifierItem tray host for the icon."
Optional: a display-shape resolver (kanshi-autoscale) for per-shape sizing.
.SH SETUP
.B ./setup.sh install
links the shell tools + the mako config;
.B ./setup.sh service
builds the tray-icon venv and enables its daemon;
.B ./setup.sh check
audits the install. See the README.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mako (1),
.BR makoctl (1)
